 $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](images/4a/4a6517f5b42ed2ffd18522ce13d817c3094245c650c41d0f456116914c818436.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. It's clear from the picture below that if we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/38/38868b69ae1836844a279e141d83b886f386c87edeedbb1e2067ffd18d7f1af3.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id 17592186259816 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186179739 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dab6bfb9-608d-5ff8-88e7-5aa9612acda4" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Constant Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "260bff3d-623d-5c25-9d39-6acf7b56a7a4" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id 17592186257110} {:answer/id #uuid "3b09af04-b07e-5d70-b1c9-a51ae8ce385a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id 17592186257308} {:answer/id #uuid "53133303-3b90-587d-bdde-cc3b9b911f4c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id 17592186257492} {:answer/id #uuid "74ff3163-bb7f-50b6-9fb2-0d96e77fd070" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :ans