tement III is false. It's clear from the picture below that if we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/41/41528079b285fb3ba20fcac0bd28f42ed7981a775938286654cf7319c1e8a6c6.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id 17592186259817 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186179742 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d72127a-90d6-5f7e-bd87-75d03285a918" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Non-Constant Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00a4b86e-c031-5cff-bfab-db15503d9f66" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id 17592186256788} {:answer/id #uuid "0a29235c-0bfa-54ed-abf8-c3c828db2428" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id 17592186256874} {:answer/id #uuid "4355cd34-d70b-516a-82af-80e1bac5802b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id 17592186257375} {:answer/id #uuid "a42aceaf-50b6-55f7-b5f3-ca3c94c89c43" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id 17592186258216} {:answer/id #uuid "b8080145-c386-5251-9bd4-975eee6a779b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id 17592186258392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a29235c-0bfa-54ed-abf8-c3c828db2428" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id 17592186256874} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ca8e92d-14cf-5963-9c83-3421893b9e67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186259218}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uu