- The first set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The second set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The third set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id 17592186278579 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186192767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7adf2c3e-4a73-5098-ab60-790d637728cf" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets in the Plane in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "018bc100-91aa-543a-936f-53e746dca2fa" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id 17592186275489} {:answer/id #uuid "195e644d-a593-5f9b-af66-b2aa1bce32c8" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id 17592186275714} {:answer/id #uuid "26adde98-a760-53b4-92f0-8185d373a841" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id 17592186275828} {:answer/id #uuid "6b905fcf-9f51-5621-8ee6-8290966ae390" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id 17592186276442} {:answer/id #uuid "f6255c1f-fd9d-576d-b0e6-6836e1b6e132" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id 17592186277633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "195e644d-a593-5f9b-af66-b2aa1bce32c8" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id 17592186275714} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a32781a-dbff-5332-93de-1878429e1d51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186277745}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "168b395c-d069-5c8f-9acc-5bed4b37b963" :question/math-academy-id "q-161642" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are closed?\n\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}\\le 1}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2x-{x}^{2}}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 3}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The second set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The third set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id 17592186278581 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186192767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7adf2c3e-4a73-5098-ab60-790d637728cf" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets in the Plane in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fa6cde3-1ae8-5afa-8dd7-e176e90cdc8a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id 17592186275902} {:answer/id #uuid "36daff44-c75d-5e4b-84a4-fc89decd9d95" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id 17592186275965} {:answer/id #uuid "8317ebc3-52a8-5268-806e-9ea55699a12d" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/val