on each $[0,2]$  and $[2,5].$\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."}] [{:db/id 17592186341985 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186175903 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bbc6a2d-2078-50d5-9584-c705c19212da" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Intervals on Which a Given Function Satisfies the Extreme Value Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24811889-2c2a-5489-87b6-7ec9fcc9ec5d" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id 17592186339445} {:answer/id #uuid "49559a38-7682-51c6-961d-af8f6d4b9c7c" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id 17592186339786} {:answer/id #uuid "8e550649-e7ec-521f-b83e-ccfcdfe9298e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id 17592186340407} {:answer/id #uuid "b182cd8c-78d4-5443-bfc8-d64291dce17e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id 17592186340743} {:answer/id #uuid "b2f9dc50-f6a9-5e82-a931-a20f17095169" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id 17592186340755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b182cd8c-78d4-5443-bfc8-d64291dce17e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id 17592186340743} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cc71ef4-f030-5214-97b4-d07a1eb70ea5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186341431}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fe7192f0-0469-5c77-92a1-060194834d30" :question/math-academy-id "q-73482" :question/problem "On which of the following intervals can the extreme value theorem be applied to the function $y=\\frac{x-1}{\\sqrt{x+1}}?$   \n\n- $[-1,0]$\n- $[1,10]$\n- $(-1,0)$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous. \n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at each interval.\n\n- The interval $[-1,0]$ is closed, but the function is not continuous on it because it is not defined at $x=-1.$  Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[1,10]$ is  closed, and the function is continuous on $[1,10].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\n- The interval  $(-1,0)$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id 17592186341986 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186175903 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bbc6a2d-2078-50d5-9584-c705c19212da" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Intervals on Which a Given Function Satisfies the Extreme Value Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a68717c-3c5f-58a5-9174-e8f45f3e1ef1" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id 17592186339216} {:answer/id #uuid "336f07da-9df2-582d-80ca-e44d8eb292b0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id 17592186339585} {:answer/id #uuid "43af0409-9e51-5d17-a8fb-98b37bd00bec" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id 17592186339722} {:answer/id #uuid "72581646-406e-5e01-9bba-7ad77de94142" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id 17592186340144} {:answer/id #uuid "8e33f721-3fb7-5e44-8644-c40ab2c07185" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id 17592186340406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "336f07da-9df2-582d-80ca-e44d8eb292b0" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id 17592186339585} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a35e850-44d5-5740-b0b8-70909d0b180d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186341650}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5aba1141-c0a4-54c1-bd64-30eb78786676" :question/math-academy-id "q-73484" :question/problem "On which of the following intervals can the extreme value theorem be applied to the function $y=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}?$    \n\nI. $[\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ]$\n\nII. $[\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{2})$\n\nIII. $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous. \n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at each interval.\n\n- The interval $[\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ]$  is closed, but the function is not defined on a part of the interval because $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)<0$ for all $x\\in (\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{2})$    is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]$ is  closed, and the function is continuous on $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id 17592186341987 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186175903 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bbc6a2d-2078-50d5-9584-c705c19212da" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Intervals on Which a Given Function Satisfies the Extreme Value Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51327576-3dc9-528f-9e13-d755abf55471" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id 17592186339872} {:answer/id #uuid "7b3f93d2-0ebe-5934-8c91-fce10e0d1450" :answer/type {:db/id 175921