}\n$$\n\nIt does not matter whether the antecedent is true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our consequents in turn.\n\n- Predicate I, defined for $n\\in Z,$ is *not* always true. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Predicate II, defined for $n\\in Z,$ is always true. $\\,✓$\n\n- Predicate III, defined for $n\\in Z,$ is always false. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id 17592186384698 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186157232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb4d348b-1703-51a1-be05-2e66295cacaa" :knowledge-point/title "Completing Trivial Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36c987c2-5e29-5216-9447-9e1425673da8" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id 17592186384700} {:answer/id #uuid "e7a86298-d9fc-5f7b-8767-f0f77a6d7e2b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id 17592186384701} {:answer/id #uuid "777afe05-5a59-51fe-be45-ed3eaee579bd" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id 17592186384702} {:answer/id #uuid "fba134c2-9816-5ade-ad0d-bbfae0a7f342" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id 17592186384703} {:answer/id #uuid "b9c04bc7-1912-5b7b-9c92-c50c4da04ded" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id 17592186384704}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7a86298-d9fc-5f7b-8767-f0f77a6d7e2b" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id 17592186384701} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf6810a7-e363-5341-81e3-886da735f941" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186384699}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f7628b