e correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id 17592186419538 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186157308 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f0a57c2-bbad-5225-976b-385c7f117738" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Random Variables that Follow a Poisson Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d4df288-3de3-5913-80c1-82e310e1702f" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id 17592186419433} {:answer/id #uuid "46289e15-5ed5-53d3-bfb5-9ed125b4b357" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id 17592186419451} {:answer/id #uuid "6a3664a7-7754-5c55-8474-a12a38720c86" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id 17592186419457} {:answer/id #uuid "a3aceabe-b268-5af7-9a02-b0e18dbda4bc" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id 17592186419479} {:answer/id #uuid "ba905bc7-fb9a-5aee-98c6-60c46a28c15a" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id 17592186419483}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3aceabe-b268-5af7-9a02-b0e18dbda4bc" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id 17592186419479} :answer-field/id #uuid "be7fedf2-2106-5faf-a3ef-836ba7bad8ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186419528}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "71278ae0-44f4-58f6-827b-4b9773ebb613" :question/math-academy-id "q-89222" :question/problem "Which of the following random variables could be modeled using a Poisson distribution?\n\n- The number of emails received by a company's server in one week\n- The number of people who visit a coffee shop per hour\n- The height of $5$ buildings in New York City" :question/worked-solution "A Poisson distribution models the number of events that occur in an interval of time or space if events occur independently and at a constant average rate.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given random variables.\n\n- Random variable I follows a Poisson distribution. The number of emails received by a company's server can be modeled as independent events with a constant average rate, and we wish to know how many events occur in an interval of time (one week).\n\n- Random variable II follows a Poisson distribution. The number of people who visit a coffee shop can be modeled as independent events with a constant average rate, and we wish to know how many events occur in an interval of time (one hour).\n\n- Random variable III does *not* follow a Poisson distribution. There are no events that occur at a constant average rate, and there is no interval of time or space.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id 17592186419541 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186157308 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f0a57c2-bbad-5225-976b-385c7f117738" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Random Variables that Follow a Poisson Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07160410-a73d-5491-ac7b-6d22b8d2282e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id 17592186419431} {:answer/id #uuid "207e7398-1d2d-564f-924d-9241209c572e" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id 17592186419439} {:answer/id #uuid "93d90b19-71ca-57e8-931e-35cadfebadbf" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id 17592186419471} {:answer/id #uuid "bd12d504-3244-5d03-bea3-5eee58c7022d" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id 17592186419487} {:answer/id #